Thought: The all-conv-3x3 architecture gives 0.901987. That's a good baseline. Let me try some variations. Known good architectures in NAS-Bench-201 often have a mix. Let me try the optimal-ish configurations. A known strong config in NAS-Bench-201 for CIFAR-10 involves nor_conv_3x3 on several edges with skip connections. Let me try a few diverse ones.

Let me try a mix with skip connections and 1x1 convs.

Action: evaluate_config {"1<-0": "nor_conv_3x3", "2<-0": "nor_conv_1x1", "2<-1": "skip_connect", "3<-0": "nor_conv_3x3", "3<-1": "nor_conv_3x3", "3<-2": "skip_connect"}

Thought: The mixed config performed slightly worse (0.8969) than all-conv-3x3 (0.9020). Convolution-heavy architectures seem better. Let me try a configuration with more 3x3 convs but vary a couple edges. Let me try replacing some with 1x1 convs which keep performance but reduce cost, or try all 1x1.

Let me try: mostly 3x3 with one variation. Actually, since all-3x3 gave the best so far, let me explore around it. Try changing edge 2<-1 to skip_connect (common in good cells).

